+# HAL Engine tool input validation
+
+| Field  | Value |
+| ------ | ----- |
+| Issue  | #37   |
+| Status | Draft |
+
+`ToolRegistry.execute` validates `input` against the resolved tool definition's `inputSchema` before the executor runs. A rejection is returned as a `ToolResponse`, never thrown; only an unknown tool name throws.
+
+- Input missing a required property is rejected with a result naming that property, and the executor is never invoked ([validated by: rejects input missing a required property without running the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L25)).
+- A wrong-typed field is rejected with a result naming the field path and expected type, and neither the result nor any log line contains the offending value ([validated by: rejects a wrong-typed field naming its path and expected type, never its value](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L35)).
+- A schema that cannot be compiled makes `register` throw at registration time, with a message naming the tool ([validated by: throws at register time for an uncompilable schema, naming the tool](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L52)).
+- A function-valued definition is validated against the schema it returns at that call, not a stale cached one ([validated by: validates a function-valued definition against the schema current at that call](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L59)).
